1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,944
Is TypeScript catching up with JavaScript
on GitHub?

2
00:00:03,194 --> 00:00:08,077
As a share of JavaScript, yes, and
quickly; in raw numbers, no: JavaScript's

3
00:00:08,077 --> 00:00:08,719
lead grew.

4
00:00:08,969 --> 00:00:13,689
Every quarter, GitHub counts the
developers in each economy who push to

5
00:00:13,689 --> 00:00:18,807
repositories containing each language; a
repository that holds both languages

6
00:00:18,807 --> 00:00:19,871
counts for both.

7
00:00:20,121 --> 00:00:24,217
We follow the 92 economies reported for
both in every quarter.

8
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:30,749
In the first quarter of 2020, TypeScript
had 18% as many pushers as JavaScript.

9
00:00:30,999 --> 00:00:34,690
By the first quarter of 2026, it had 49%.

10
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:40,853
In raw numbers, though, JavaScript's lead
grew, from 1.1 million to 2.5 million

11
00:00:40,853 --> 00:00:43,623
pushers, because both languages grew.

12
00:00:43,873 --> 00:00:49,614
GitHub's Octoverse 2025 report named
TypeScript the most used language on

13
00:00:49,614 --> 00:00:53,153
GitHub in August 2025, by contributor
counts.

14
00:00:53,403 --> 00:00:56,795
That is a different count from the
quarterly pushers in this video.

15
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:04,329
Over the 6 years, TypeScript pushers grew
9.5 times over, and JavaScript pushers 3.4

16
00:01:04,329 --> 00:01:04,831
times.

17
00:01:05,081 --> 00:01:09,055
Among the 10 languages with the most
pushers, the fastest growing was

18
00:01:09,055 --> 00:01:09,689
TypeScript.

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:15,462
The ratio moved fastest in the last year:
it rose 12 percentage points, against at

20
00:01:15,462 --> 00:01:18,349
most 5 percentage points in any earlier
year.

21
00:01:18,867 --> 00:01:21,704
Economy by economy, the picture is the
same.

22
00:01:21,954 --> 00:01:29,322
TypeScript reached 50% of JavaScript's
pushers in 47 of the 92 economies, up from

23
00:01:29,322 --> 00:01:30,231
0 in 2020.

24
00:01:30,481 --> 00:01:32,828
The highest ratio was 61%.

25
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:39,661
Limits: GitHub omits economies with too
few active developers; those reported for

26
00:01:39,661 --> 00:01:43,723
TypeScript rose from 93 to 162, hence the
fixed set.

27
00:01:43,973 --> 00:01:49,390
Only public repositories count, developers
can count under both, and location comes

28
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:50,565
from IP addresses.

29
00:01:50,815 --> 00:01:52,991
The data shows how many pushed, not why.

30
00:01:53,241 --> 00:01:56,227
Source: GitHub's Innovation Graph, public
domain.
